.TH CSORT_GET_DEFAULT_COMPARISON_PROC 3 "2026-07-10" "c_collections" "C Collections Library - Macros"
.SH NAME
csort_get_default_comparison_proc \- get default comparison for a type
.SH LIBRARY
C Collections (libccollections, \-lccollections)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <csort.h>

ccol_comparison_proc_t csort_get_default_comparison_proc(dummy_var);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.nf
Returns the default comparison function for a given type. Uses C11
_Generic to select the appropriate comparison based on the type of the
dummy variable.

Supports all standard C integral types (char, signed char, short, int,
long, long long, unsigned variants) and floating-point types (float,
double, long double), as well as strings (char*, const char*).

A fixed-size char array (char[N]), as opposed to a char* pointer variable,
is not a supported type and returns NULL, the same as any other
unsupported type; such an array's own inline byte content is not a char*
value, so csort_default_string_comparison_proc's pointer-dereferencing
contract does not apply to it. Sort a collection of fixed-size string
buffers with an explicit, hand-written comparator passed directly to
cvector_sort_with_comparison_proc() / csort_sort() instead.
.fi
.SH PARAMETERS
.nf
dummy_var  A variable of the type you want to compare (not evaluated)
.fi
.SH RETURN VALUE
.nf
Returns pointer to appropriate comparison function
Returns NULL if type is not supported
.fi
.SH NOTES
.nf
Variable is only used for type deduction, not evaluated; dummy_var may be
any expression of the type you want to compare, including an rvalue
(a cast, a literal, ...), not only an addressable variable
For a genuine char* / const char* pointer variable, returns
csort_default_string_comparison_proc
For a fixed-size char array (char[N]), returns NULL, not
csort_default_string_comparison_proc
For integral types, uses three-way comparison: (a > b) - (a < b)
For floating-point types (float, double, long double), a NaN operand
compares greater than every non-NaN value and equal only to another NaN,
so the result is always a genuine total order
.fi
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
// Get comparator for strings
char* dummy_str;
ccol_comparison_proc_t cmp = csort_get_default_comparison_proc(dummy_str);
// cmp now points to csort_default_string_comparison_proc

// Get comparator for doubles
double dummy_double;
cmp = csort_get_default_comparison_proc(dummy_double);
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR csort_sort (3),
.BR cvec_sort (3)
